BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Sacred Spring) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  In ancient times, two villages were separated by a barren valley. The gods placed between them) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (     a Sacred Spring with a peculiar blessing: any water poured into it from one side would flow) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (     to the other, tripled in abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  The First Village discovered this gift. A young farmer, though thirsty, poured half his water ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    into the Spring. It flowed across, becoming enough to nourish the Second Village's entire ha) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    rvest. Grateful, they poured back even more than they received.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  Soon the villages prospered, each pouring generously, each receiving abundance threefold. The ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    Spring became a symbol of their bond-trust transformed into prosperity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  But one summer, fear whispered in hearts. "What if they keep it all?" some worried. "Why shoul) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    d we give when we might receive nothing?" A few held back their water. Seeing less flow thei) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    r way, the other village grew cautious too.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (  The Spring still worked its magic, but with little poured in, little multiplied. The valley gr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    ew dry again.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (  An elder reminded them: "The Spring multiplies what we offer in trust. Its true magic is not t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (    he tripling, but the bond it creates. Pour generously, return fairly, and both villages flou) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.0 Tf 48.0 24.0 Td (Page 5 of 300) Tj ET
