BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      # The Parable of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages shared a valley divided by a dry riverbed. Each week, the R) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        iver Spirit blessed one village with five urns of sacred water.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      The blessed village faced a choice: pour their water into the dry riverbed, or keep it for) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (         themselves. When water flowed into the riverbed, the River Spirit would triple it, send) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        ing it downstream to the other village. That village could then choose how much to send ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        back upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      At first, both villages hoarded their water, fearing betrayal. Their crops withered, and t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        rust died.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      Then a wise elder poured all five urns into the riverbed. Fifteen urns reached the downstr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        eam village. Their people, moved by this faith, sent back eight urns. Both villages pros) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        pered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      Over time, they learned: generosity multiplied by magic creates abundance, but only when m) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        et with gratitude. The one who gives first shows courage. The one who receives must hono) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        r that courage with fairness, or the river runs dry forever.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      The River Spirit whispered: "Trust is the water that feeds both wells. Send it forward, re) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (        turn it justly, and neither shall thirst.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
